<h3>2. Batch Size</h3>
<p>
  Most speculative decoding papers report results at batch size 1. This is the latency-critical
  setting (e.g., interactive chatbots), but many production deployments run larger batches for
  throughput. The problem: draft overhead becomes proportionally larger as the target model's
  utilization rises with batch size. At batch=32, the target model is no longer memory-bandwidth
  bound — it's compute-bound — so the verification "free ride" disappears.
</p>

